deliverables/sources/SRC-TIME-01.txt:32:L29:      * Transparency rules (Article 50) start to apply.
deliverables/sources/SRC-TIME-01.txt:38:L35: New prohibitions + Article 50(2) transition apply **
deliverables/sources/SRC-TIME-01.txt:40:L37:      * Transitional deadline for certain providers of AI systems, including GPAI systems, generating synthetic content, that were already placed on the market before 02 Aug 2026, to comply with Article 50(2).
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:15:L12: According to Article 50(2) of the AI Act, providers must design and develop AI systems that interact directly with natural persons — such as chatbots, AI agents, and avatars — to ensure that people are informed they are interacting with AI. Providers must also ensure that the outputs of their generative AI systems are marked with effective, reliable, robust and interoperable machine-readable marks that enable the outputs to be detected as generated or manipulated by AI systems.
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:25:L22: When do providers of AI systems have to inform people they are interacting with an AI system?
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:26:L23: According to cite1†Article 50(1) of the AI Act†ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu , Providers of AI systems that directly interact with people must design and develop those systems in such a way that the individuals concerned are informed that they are interacting with an AI system, unless this is obvious.
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:44:L41: When do providers of AI systems have to mark the outputs of their generative AI systems and ensure their detectability?
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:45:L42: According to cite1†Article 50(2) of the AI Act†ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu , providers of AI systems, including general-purpose AI systems, generating synthetic audio, image, video or text content, must ensure that AI-generated or manipulated content are marked in a machine-readable format and detectable as artificially generated or manipulated.
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:56:L53: To ensure Article 50(2) of the AI Act is implemented in a proportionate manner, a narrow exemption of the marking obligation is envisaged for AI systems that generate outputs used in “business to business” or “industrial contexts” (provided the conditions specified in the guidelines are met).
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:115:L112: The cite3†Code of Practice on Transparency of AI-generated content provides a voluntary practical tool to help providers and deployers of generative AI systems demonstrate compliance with the marking and labelling obligations under cite1†Article 50(2), (4) and (5) of the AI Act†ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu . The code has been assessed as adequate by both the Commission and the AI Board.
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:117:L114: Providers and deployers of generative AI systems that decide not to adhere to the code will have to demonstrate compliance through alternative adequate means. They may be subject to more requests for information, since there is less transparency on how they comply with the transparency obligations of Article 50(2), (4) and (5) of the AI Act.
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:118:L115: For the other transparency obligations (e.g. those laid down in Article 50(1) and (3) of the AI Act), providers and deployers can determine adequate compliance measures themselves, while taking into account the cite2†Guidelines on Transparency of AI-Generated Content .
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:126:L123: cite1†Article 50 of the AI Act†ai-act-service-desk.ec.europa.eu applies as from 2 August 2026. From that date onwards, providers and deployers of AI systems must comply with the transparency obligations laid down in that provision. A limited grace period is envisaged only for AI systems placed on the market before 2 August 2026 and only as regards the marking and detection obligation for AI-generated content (Article 50(2) of the AI Act).
deliverables/sources/SRC-FAQ-01.txt:136:L133: 24 July 2026
deliverables/sources/SRC-LAW-01.txt:93:L224: The text displayed here is based on the cite313†EUR-Lex consolidated version of the AI Act as at 27 July 2026†eur-lex.europa.eu . Where shown, “NEW” and “AMENDED” identify passages containing additions or amendments to the cite314†original AI Act†eur-lex.europa.eu made by the cite315†Digital Omnibus on AI†eur-lex.europa.eu . For more information, refer to cite316†the FAQ section under 'Digital Omnibus' .
